          %h1#tensor_products_of_banach_spaces Tensor products of Banach spaces
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#cross_norms"} Cross norms
              %li
                %a{:href => "#schmidt_decomposition"} Schmidt decomposition
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#theorem_nielsen_and_chuang_theorem_27"} Theorem
                  %a{:href => "#NielsenChuang"} (Nielsen and Chuang Theorem 2.7)
              %li
                %a{:href => "#foundational_issues"} Foundational issues
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_pages"} Related pages
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There are various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norms"} norms
            that may be placed on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            of two
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+space"} complete
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion"} completion
            = succeed "," do
              %em projective tensor product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ban"} Ban
            (the category of Banach spaces and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+linear+maps"} short linear maps
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+symmetric+monoidal+category"} closed symmetric monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ban
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ban
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilb"} Hilb
            also becomes a symmetric monoidal category.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
            be their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            as Banach spaces, we will place a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+space"} normed vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mover
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V {\displaystyle\hat{\otimes}} W
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_projective_tensor_product Definition (projective tensor product)
            %p
              Every element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              may be written (in many different ways) as a formal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
              of formal tensor products of elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              (suppressing the symbol
              = succeed "):" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi i
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_i \alpha_i v_i w_i .
            %p
              Let the
              %strong projective cross norm
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x\|_\pi}
              of an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              be
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi π
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi inf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi W
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x\|_\pi} \coloneqq \inf \{ \sum_i {|\alpha_i|} {\|v_i\|_V} {\|w_i\|_W} \;|\; x = \sum_i \alpha_i v_i w_i \} .
            %p
              Then the
              %strong projective tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mi π
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V {\displaystyle\hat{\otimes}_\pi} W
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is the completion of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              under the projective cross norm.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_injective_tensor_product Definition (injective tensor product)
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functionals"} linear functionals
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              (respectively), then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \otimes \mu
              is a linear functional on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              %strong injective cross norm
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x\|_\epsilon}
              of an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              be
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi ϵ
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi λ
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi λ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi V
                            %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi W
                            %mo *
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x\|_\epsilon} \coloneqq \sup \{ {|(\lambda \otimes \mu)x|} \;|\; {\|\lambda\|_{V^*}}, {\|\mu\|_{W^*}} \leq 1 \} .
            %p
              Then the
              %strong injective tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mi ϵ
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V {\displaystyle\hat{\otimes}_\epsilon} W
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is the completion of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              under the injective cross norm.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_tensor_product_of_hilbert_spaces Definition (tensor product of Hilbert spaces)
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+products"} inner products
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              are generated by elements of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v w
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle{v_1 w_1, v_2 w_2}\rangle \coloneqq \langle{v_1, v_2}\rangle \langle{w_1, w_2}\rangle
            %p
              and extend by linearity. We write the norm of an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x\|_\sigma}
              %strong tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mi σ
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V {\displaystyle\hat{\otimes}_\sigma} W
              of the Hilbert spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is the completion of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              under this norm (or inner product).
          %h2#cross_norms Cross norms
          %p
            Besides the specific norms defined above, we can define axioms of a reasonable norm on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_cross_norm Definition (cross norm)
            %p
              A
              %strong cross norm
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is
              %em any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              such that:
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi w
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi χ
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi w
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|v \otimes w\|_\chi} = {\|v\|_V} {\|w\|_W}
                for any elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                (respectively);
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi λ
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi χ
                              %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi λ
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi V
                              %mo *
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi W
                              %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|\lambda \otimes \mu\|_{\chi^*}} = {\|\lambda\|_{V^*}} {\|\mu\|_{W^*}}
                for any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+linear+functionals"} bounded linear functionals
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                (respectively).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_uniform_cross_norm Definition (uniform cross norm)
            %p
              A
              %strong uniform cross norm
              is an operation that takes two Banach spaces and returns a norm on their algebraic tensor product,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturally
              in the two spaces. Equivalently, it's a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ban
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ban
                    %mo →
                    %mi NVect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi\colon Ban \times Ban \to NVect
              that makes the following diagram commute (or fills it with a
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ban
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Ban
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi χ
                          %mtd
                            %mi NVect
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Vect
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Vect
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mo ⊗
                          %mtd
                            %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array { Ban \times Ban   &amp; \overset{\chi}\rightarrow     &amp; NVect \\
                    \\downarrow       &amp;                               &amp; \downarrow \\
                    Vect \times Vect &amp; \underset{\otimes}\rightarrow &amp; Vect
                    }
          %p
            A uniform cross norm is obviously desirable from the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p A uniform cross norm assigns a cross norm to any two Banach spaces.
          %p The specific cross norms from the previous section qualify as much as possible:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p The projective and injective cross norms are uniform cross norms (and hence are in fact cross norms). The norm on the algebraic tensor product of two Hilbert spaces is also a cross norm.
          %p
            As far as I can tell, the Hilbert-space cross norm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            doesn't apply to arbitrary Banach spaces, so it doesn't define a uniform cross norm as defined above; however, it does define a functor on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hilb
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Hilb
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hilb \times Hilb
          %p Looking only at the general theory of cross norms, the projective and injective cross norms appear naturally:
          #topbot.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_ryan_2002_prop_61
              Proposition
              %a{:href => "#Ryan02"} (Ryan 2002, Prop. 6.1)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              be Banach spaces and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
              be any norm on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
              is a cross norm if and only if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi ϵ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi χ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi π
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x\|_\epsilon} \leq {\|x\|_\chi} \leq {\|x\|_\pi},
            %p
              for every
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in V \otimes W
          %p
            That is, we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            of cross norms, and the projective and injective cross norms are (respectively) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top"} top
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom"} bottom
            of this poset.
          %p
            We therefore obtain the following relationship between
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
          .num_prop
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              are Hilbert spaces and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is an element of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi ϵ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi σ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi π
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x\|_\epsilon} \leq {\|x\|_\sigma} \leq {\|x\|_\pi} .
          %p
            Of course, any cross norm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            allows us to form the Banach space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mi χ
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V {\displaystyle\hat{\otimes}_\chi} W
            %strong tensor product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %h2#schmidt_decomposition Schmidt decomposition
          %p
            The
            %strong Schmidt decomposition
            is a way of expressing a pure state in the tensor product of two Hilbert spaces in terms of states of the two components:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_nielsen_and_chuang_theorem_27
              Theorem
              %a{:href => "#NielsenChuang"} (Nielsen and Chuang Theorem 2.7)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              be finite-dimensional Hilbert spaces. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\psi\rangle
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+state"} pure state
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B
              %span.newWikiWord
                orthonormal families
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/orthonormal+family"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ |i_A \rangle \}_i
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ |i_B \rangle \}_i
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\psi\rangle = \sum_i \lambda_i |i_A \rangle \otimes |i_B\rangle
            %p
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                      %msubsup
                        %mi λ
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_i \lambda_i^2 = 1
          %p
            The numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_i
            are called the
            %strong Schmidt co-efficients
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\psi\rangle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ |i_A\rangle \}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ |i_B\rangle \}
            the
            %strong Schmidt bases
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong Schmidt number
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\psi\rangle
              is the number of non-zero Schmidt coefficients of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\psi\rangle
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Although most often stated for finite dimensional Hilbert spaces, the Schmidt decomposition theorem stated as above works for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              Hilbert spaces of arbitrary dimension (even uncountable). A proof follows through a straightforward application of the polar decomposition and spectral theorems to the positive trace-class operator given by the partial trace of the projection operator onto
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
              (see
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a{:href => "#MO20960"} MO: Schmidt Decomposition on infinite-dimensional Hilbert spaces
          %h2#foundational_issues Foundational issues
          %p
            We need the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hahn%E2%80%93Banach+theorem"} Hahn–Banach theorem
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            to be a cross norm; but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            work regardless. Possibly some of the other propositions rely on some other form of the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
